From ac091b2726580a3ffd527a97edd8ef22fb68005a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:37:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homar theme wallpapers: pick the phone's lock and home
 wallpapers from the Omarchy theme

A "Wallpaper from Omarchy" settings screen. On top, two mini phones show the lock screen (clock and
date) and the home screen (this phone's own dock and apps) as the draft would make them, each with
its darken/lighten layer. A segmented "Lock screen / Home screen / Both" says which screen(s) the
choice is for (the previews light up; tapping a preview picks that screen). Below, three tabs:
Current (keep what the screen shows; the phone's own wallpaper when Android lets it be read, else
its wallpaper colours), Omarchy (the theme's backgrounds) and Gradients (made from the theme's
colours by the computer). Taps only change the draft; the bottom bar's Apply sends one choice per
screen (launcher.theme_wallpaper_choice {at, screens}) and shows how it goes (Applying, waiting for
the unlock, computer not reachable, failed); Discard returns to what is applied. The computer
pushes the list (launcher.theme_wallpapers_set: items, gradients, screens, layer, thumbnails) and
answers (launcher.theme_wallpaper_ack). Hooks: the three methods in OmalawnCommands and LinkServer,
one route line in PreferenceNavigation and one row in PreferencesDashboard.

The choice read also answers needs_list while this process has no list in the current format (the
home screen restarted, often for an app update, or the list on disk is the older format the
computer sent an older build), so the computer sends the whole list again; launcher.ping carries
installed_at (the package's lastUpdateTime), because our builds share one version. A failed ack
with code wallpaper_unsaved (the current wallpaper cannot be saved first) shows only the question
"Replace current wallpaper?"; Replace sends the same choice with overwrite, Cancel keeps it as the
draft. Every word on the screen is our own English string (Apply included), never a translated one.
